  steps: [
    { math: '1 · The NPK core', note: 'Nitrogen (leaf growth — the volatile one, easily lost), phosphorus (roots, flowering — the finite one), potassium (stress tolerance, fruit quality). The macro trio on every fertiliser bag; secondary (Ca, Mg, S) and micros complete the diet.' },
    { math: '2 · The 4Rs of application', note: 'Right source, right rate, right time, right place — the industry\'s framework for getting nutrients into the crop instead of the watercourse. Timing to growth stages; placement near roots; slow-release coatings.' },
    { math: '3 · The yield-response curve (the lesson\'s law again)', note: 'The foundational lesson\'s diminishing returns ARE fertiliser economics: the last kg of nitrogen pays less than the first, and past the optimum it costs yield (lodging) and money (the agronomy lesson\'s curve, managed).' },
    { math: '4 · The runoff bill', note: 'Excess N and P feed algae — the water lesson\'s dead zones; nitrate in drinking water. Precision agriculture (the coming lesson) exists largely to shave this bill: the environmental cost of the flat part of the curve.' },
  ],
};
